### Book CRUD
### Start PostgreSQL first (`docker compose up -d` from 02-bookstore-capstone/), then
### `./mvnw spring-boot:run`, then execute these top to bottom.
### Every endpoint is public at this stage; Step 3 adds JWT and the ADMIN role.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. List books (paged, seeded with 5 rows under the dev profile)
GET {{host}}/api/books

### 2. List with paging and sorting
GET {{host}}/api/books?page=0&size=2&sort=price,desc

### 3. Keyword search over the title
GET {{host}}/api/books?keyword=java

### 4. Get one book -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/books/1

### 5. Get a missing book -> 404 with the ErrorResponse envelope
GET {{host}}/api/books/9999

### 6. Create a book with an author -> 201 + Location header
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Refactoring",
  "isbn": "9780134757599",
  "price": 47.99,
  "stock": 10,
  "authorId": 2
}

### 6b. authorId is optional — a book with no author on record -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Anonymous Manual",
  "isbn": "9999999999999",
  "price": 9.99,
  "stock": 1
}

### 6c. A non-existent authorId is a client error, not a silently-dropped field -> 404
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost",
  "isbn": "8888888888888",
  "price": 9.99,
  "stock": 1,
  "authorId": 9999
}

### 7. Create with a duplicate ISBN -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Refactoring (again)",
  "isbn": "9780134757599",
  "price": 47.99,
  "stock": 1
}

### 8. Create with invalid fields -> 400 with per-field messages
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "price": -5,
  "stock": -1
}

### 9. Update a book -> 200
PUT {{host}}/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code (2nd printing)",
  "isbn": "9780132350884",
  "price": 39.99,
  "stock": 20
}

### 10. Update a missing book -> 404
PUT {{host}}/api/books/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost",
  "price": 10.00,
  "stock": 1
}

### 11. Delete a book -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/5

### 12. Delete it again -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/5

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 2c — the N+1 demonstration
### Watch the application log with SQL logging on (dev profile) while running
### these two. Identical responses, very different query counts.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 13. Authors with their books — one LEFT JOIN FETCH -> 1 query
GET {{host}}/api/authors

### 14. The same data, the naive way -> 1 + N queries (6 with the seed data)
GET {{host}}/api/authors?naive=true
